issues.description:
The 13-letter calibration understates the gain from L. The attacker's run had n=12, and all 12 enumerations were time-limited, incomplete, and never contained the truth. It found a mean change of -0.13 (SE 0.15) and called it not significant. Its sign-test p of 0.07 is one-sided and was not labelled as such; two-sided p = 0.146. The report says exact-hit rates are unchanged.
My rerun used the same tool: seed 2718, 5,000 words, 90 s, n=16 (review/calib_c13.json):
- mean -0.404 (SE 0.134, t = -3.0); 13 improved, 3 worse; two-sided p = 0.021;
- top-1 hits 0 -> 3; median rank 492 -> 136.
Pooled (n=28): mean -0.286 (SE 0.101); 22 improved, 6 worse; two-sided sign test p = 0.004; top-1 hits 1 -> 4.
In-model, L gives a modest but statistically significant improvement in rank, about 1.9x. This is still a best case:
- the same model generates and scores the ciphers;
- the 10-distinct-symbol filter keeps mostly S = 20-35;
- lists are still mostly incomplete.
The conclusion that L singles out no plaintext stands.

The simulation check is reported only with the real key sizes, which is an in-sample check. With model-drawn key sizes, which is what the Z13/Z32 inference actually uses, several statistics fall outside the 5-95% band (fit.log):
- Z340 repeatBigrams: 25 vs p95 24 (percentile 0.967);
- Z408 part 3 cycleRate: percentile 0.02;
- Z408 part 3 near_d2: percentile 0.992.

The caveat about truncated lists is wrong in detail:
- enum_z13_circles_distinct_SIMPLE also stopped at 60 s (complete=false), so the word-list evidence for circles_distinct is a lower bound on both sides;
- enum_z13_reversed_homophonic completed in 38 s;
- the canonical homophonic list (3.72M strings) is incomplete, so its homophonic evidence is a lower bound.
The complete names list gives Bayes factor 10^3.31, not 10^3.8.

Several hypotheses were not tested:
- resets at section/part boundaries, separately from per-row resets (tau ties every row boundary together);
- a non-English or numeric Z32 plaintext (the July 26 letter mentions radians and inches), which bears on the Z32 S and regime posteriors;
- transpositions other than reversal;
- subsets of the letters_literal pins (README 13.4 says 'or a subset');
- key-to-key persistence of single-symbol letters (M, C, G, V have k=1 in both solved keys).
